hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2780","Narrated to us Yunus bin Abd al-A'la, who informed us that Ibn Wahb informed me that Yunus (on the authority of) Ibn Shihab, who said: Ubaydullah bin Abdullah bin Utba narrated to me from Ibn Abbas (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed Tawaf during the Farewell Pilgrimage while riding a camel, and he touched the Black Stone with his staff."
"2781","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn ‘Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri’, narrated to us ‘Abdullah ibn Raja’, on the authority of Musa ibn ‘Uqbah, on the authority of ‘Abdullah ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ibn ‘Umar (RA), who said:\n\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed Tawaf on his camel"","" the Qaswa’"","" on the Day of the Conquest (of Makkah)"","" so that he could touch the Corner (the Black Stone) with his staff (Miḥjan).\""\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""""
